//~ compile_fail(backend)
//~ error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch

// NEGATIVE (must FAIL to compile): put anonymous memory behind a reservation and
// tear it down without ever touching it.
//
// This is pillar 4's asymmetry, on the half where this module applies it.
// `release` accepts <!used> or <!frozen>; both are reachable only through a real
// access or through the named escape. `commit` mints <mapped!>. So
// `commit(); release();` is not a program you can write.
//
// WHY THE COMMITTED HALF AND NOT THE RESERVED HALF. A reservation is address
// space and nothing else — no physical memory, no page-table entries
// (vma_types.h:20-35) — so `withdraw` takes <!reserved> and demands nothing, and
// tests/boot_vmem.kz's second flow does exactly that on purpose. A `commit`
// changes that: `uk_vma_map` with `uk_vma_anon_ops` installs a fault handler that
// calls the frame allocator on first touch (vma_anon.c:63). Committing and
// dropping is the one that acquires something, and it is the one that is gated.
//
// THE C HAS NOTHING TO SAY ABOUT EITHER, and could not: `uk_vma_map` followed by
// `uk_vma_unmap` over the same range is correct, warning-free, assertion-free
// and does no work. ukvmem cannot know whether the caller read the range —
// demand paging means an untouched anonymous mapping never even allocated a
// frame.
//
// THE LEGITIMATE CASE STAYS EXPRESSIBLE AND STAYS LOUD. A guard range, or a
// mapping held so a later `commit` cannot take the address, writes
// `unikraft/vmem:untouched` and compiles:
//
//     grep -r "vmem:untouched"
//
// What this refuses is the SILENT no-op.
//
// EXPECTED, verbatim: error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch: expected
//           '!unikraft.vmem:used|!unikraft.vmem:frozen' but got
//           'unikraft.vmem:mapped!' for argument 'area'

// The `unikraft` namespace is declared here, not inherited: koruc's built-in
// alias probes the sibling koru-libs CHECKOUT, so in a worktree this file would
// otherwise compile against main's lifts instead of the ones beside it.
~std/compiler:paths {
    unikraft: {{ ENTRY }}/../..
}

~import unikraft/vmem
~import std/io

~unikraft/vmem:active
| ready vm |> unikraft/vmem:reserve(vm.space, bytes: 4096)
    | area rsv |> unikraft/vmem:commit(rsv.area)
        | ok mapped |> unikraft/vmem:release(area: mapped)
            | ok |> std/io:print.ln("should never get here")
            | failed e |> unikraft/vmem:abandon(e.area)
        | refused e |> unikraft/vmem:withdraw(e.area)
            | ok |> _
            | failed x |> unikraft/vmem:abandon(x.area)
    | refused e |> std/io:print.ln("reserve failed: {{ e.reason:s }}")
| unavailable why |> std/io:print.ln("no address space: {{ why:s }}")
